<title>USA: Coca-Cola sees Q3 gain from German merger.</title>
<headline>Coca-Cola sees Q3 gain from German merger.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Coca-Cola Co said on Monday that it expects a third quarter accounting gain from the merger of its three bottlers in southern Germany with its East German bottler, but did not indicate the size of the gain.</p>
<p>As part of the previously announced merger, the revamped company will be changed to Coca-Cola Erfrischungsgetranke AG, a stock corporation that will be floated on the German stock market, the company said.</p>
<p>Shareholders of the south German bottlers will hold 55 percent of Coca-Cola Erfrischungsgetranke AG shares, and Coca-Cola will hold 45 percent through a German subsidiary.</p>
</text>
